{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T00:30:36.645Z","ordinal":78,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a19ecc-82f0-7492-9f12-a328e4f8c843","turn_id":"01a19ed0-8e84-7e53-94f4-b25b64fb9683","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_080347deb607e55e016ae92b29ce30819b9e5af59a83632820","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"If **Sun commits diverge**, `sun push` automatically creates a history join with both tips as parents:\n\n```text\n      local ──┐\nbase ─┤       ├── join\n      remote ─┘\n```\n\nThe join’s file snapshot is **exactly your local Sun snapshot**. Remote operations remain in the ancestry, but their file changes are not applied. There’s no conflict resolution.\n\nSo if remote Sun history contains an edit your local snapshot lacks, that edit stays in the historical record but is absent from the joined snapshot. **The current implementation combines provenance, not file changes.**"}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793665833764,"completed_at_ms":1793665836645}}
